@startuml MCU System Context – Bare-Metal IDS
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam actorStyle awesome

title MCU Deployment – System Context Diagram

' === External Actors ===
actor "Embedded\nDeveloper" as Dev
actor "Fleet Operator" as Fleet

' === Vehicle Network ===
package "Vehicle CAN Bus" as VehicleBus {
    node "CAN High-Speed Bus\n(500 kbps)" as CAN_HS #LightYellow
    node "CAN Low-Speed Bus\n(125 kbps)" as CAN_LS #LightYellow
}

package "CAN Bus Nodes" as Nodes {
    node "Engine\nECU" as ECU_ENG #LightCyan
    node "Transmission\nECU" as ECU_TRANS #LightCyan
    node "ABS / ESP\nECU" as ECU_ABS #LightCyan
    node "Body Control\nModule" as BCM #LightCyan
    node "OBD-II\nPort" as OBD #Orange
}

' === Target MCU ===
node "IDS MCU Board" as MCU_Board #LightGreen {
    component "CAN\nTransceiver\n(TJA1050)" as CAN_PHY
    component "ARM Cortex-M4\nMCU" as MCU_Core #PaleGreen {
    }
    component "Status LEDs\n(Normal/Attack)" as LEDs
    component "UART\n(Debug / Log)" as UART_Port
}

' === Optional external ===
node "Gateway ECU\n(optional)" as GW #Plum
node "Debugger\n(J-Link / ST-Link)" as Debugger #LightGray

' === Connections ===
ECU_ENG --> CAN_HS : Engine rpm,\ntemp, load
ECU_TRANS --> CAN_HS : Gear, speed
ECU_ABS --> CAN_HS : Wheel speed,\nbrake pressure
BCM --> CAN_LS : Door, lights,\nwindows
OBD --> CAN_HS : <<potential\nattack entry>>

CAN_HS --> CAN_PHY : CAN H/L
CAN_LS --> CAN_PHY : CAN H/L\n(dual-channel)
CAN_PHY --> MCU_Core : RX frames\n(MCAN peripheral)
MCU_Core --> CAN_PHY : TX alert\nframe (0x7FF)
MCU_Core --> LEDs : Attack indicator
MCU_Core --> UART_Port : Debug output

MCU_Board --> GW : Alert\nrelay (CAN)
GW --> CAN_HS : Block / filter\nmalicious frames

Debugger --> MCU_Board : SWD\n(flash + debug)
Dev --> Debugger : arm-none-eabi-gcc\nbuild + flash

Fleet --> GW : Remote\nmonitoring

note right of MCU_Board
  **Target hardware:**
  STM32F446RE (Cortex-M4 @ 180 MHz)
  RAM: 128 KB | Flash: 512 KB
  CAN 2.0B: 3 × CAN interfaces
  Power: 5V from vehicle harness
end note

note bottom of MCU_Core
  **IDS pipeline on-chip:**
  1. CAN RX → ring buffer (256 frames)
  2. Feature extraction (46 features)
  3. INT8 inference (TNN/LR/DT)
  4. Alert via GPIO + CAN TX
  Total memory: < 4 KB model + 8 KB app
end note

note left of OBD
  **Monitored attacks:**
  • DoS flooding
  • Fuzzy injection
  • Gear spoofing
  • RPM spoofing
end note

@enduml